# `pnpm setup` rebuilds these; the schema module in */generated/seed is committed, the Prisma Client is not.
*/generated/client/
*.db
*.db-journal
*/seed.sql
# What an example's provider.ts writes and generates to run its checks on PostgreSQL and MySQL:
# made from its schema.prisma on each run.
*/.provider/
# A local .env for a database of your own; the committed configs name the compose databases.
.env
# sqlite/ builds its tables with `prisma db push` and keeps no migration history; a directory
# there is something the Studio Migrate page wrote while it was being tried out.
sqlite/migrations/
# What `pnpm run setup` in migrate/ builds: the committed state is the two schemas, the rows and
# the decisions; the database, its history and the schema in place are made from them.
migrate/dev.db
migrate/dev.db-journal
migrate/schema.prisma
migrate/migrations/
migrate/.hekireki/
# What `pnpm run demo` in active-record/ installs beside the check: the gems and bundler's path to
# them. The models and locale files it generates are committed, to be read without running it.
active-record/vendor/
active-record/.bundle/
